WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.405 --> 00:00:06.506
These people

00:00:06.506 --> 00:00:08.008
are challenging themselves

00:00:08.008 --> 00:00:09.809
to stay underwater

00:00:09.809 --> 00:00:12.078
for as long as possible.

00:00:12.078 --> 00:00:14.981
Some go for half a day

00:00:14.981 --> 00:00:16.282
while others

00:00:16.282 --> 00:00:17.450
manage to spend

00:00:17.450 --> 00:00:20.987
an entire week fully submerged.

00:00:20.987 --> 00:00:21.888
What would happen

00:00:21.888 --> 00:00:22.922
to your body

00:00:22.922 --> 00:00:24.991
if you tried this challenge.

00:00:24.991 --> 00:00:27.894
Would your skin fall off?

00:00:27.894 --> 00:00:29.496
On today's challenge,

00:00:29.496 --> 00:00:31.731
we're going to find out.

00:00:37.270 --> 00:00:38.671
In 2006,

00:00:38.671 --> 00:00:40.707
David Blaine challenged himself

00:00:40.707 --> 00:00:42.342
to be underwater

00:00:42.342 --> 00:00:44.577
for a full seven days.

00:00:44.577 --> 00:00:46.746
He trained with the Navy SEALs

00:00:46.746 --> 00:00:48.648
to lose 23 kg (50 lb),

00:00:48.648 --> 00:00:49.816
so his body

00:00:49.816 --> 00:00:51.851
would require less oxygen.

00:00:51.851 --> 00:00:53.787
But we're dropping you

00:00:53.787 --> 00:00:54.888
into this challenge

00:00:54.888 --> 00:00:56.056
right away,

00:00:56.056 --> 00:00:58.491
with no training at all.

00:00:58.491 --> 00:00:59.559
Is this something

00:00:59.559 --> 00:01:00.660
you'd be able to handle?

00:01:02.929 --> 00:01:04.998
The moment you go underwater,

00:01:04.998 --> 00:01:07.000
you'd use less oxygen and

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:08.368
therefore could stay

00:01:08.368 --> 00:01:10.303
submerged longer.

00:01:10.303 --> 00:01:12.405
As your heart slowed down,

00:01:12.405 --> 00:01:14.240
your blood would be diverted

00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:16.142
to essential organs that

00:01:16.142 --> 00:01:17.544
need oxygen the most,

00:01:17.544 --> 00:01:19.012
like your brain,

00:01:19.012 --> 00:01:19.846
heart and,

00:01:19.846 --> 00:01:21.314
kidneys.

00:01:21.314 --> 00:01:22.282
This shunting

00:01:22.282 --> 00:01:22.916
is called

00:01:22.916 --> 00:01:25.085
peripheral vasoconstriction.

00:01:27.087 --> 00:01:29.122
Okay, you're thirty seconds in.

00:01:29.122 --> 00:01:30.290
At this point,

00:01:30.290 --> 00:01:32.092
you would want to breath again.

00:01:32.092 --> 00:01:34.661
You could keep holding your breath

00:01:34.661 --> 00:01:36.029
for two minutes

00:01:36.029 --> 00:01:37.230
if you’re trained for

00:01:37.230 --> 00:01:39.032
underwater emergencies but,

00:01:39.032 --> 00:01:40.867
past that time,

00:01:40.867 --> 00:01:41.835
you’ll need to be

00:01:41.835 --> 00:01:44.437
assisted by a breathing device.

00:01:44.437 --> 00:01:46.139
If you're a free diver,

00:01:46.139 --> 00:01:47.140
you'd be able to keep going

00:01:47.140 --> 00:01:49.342
for more than 10 minutes.

00:01:49.342 --> 00:01:50.276
To do so,

00:01:50.276 --> 00:01:51.377
you would have expelled

00:01:51.377 --> 00:01:53.646
carbon dioxide out of your lungs

00:01:53.646 --> 00:01:56.216
by hyperventilating.

00:01:56.216 --> 00:01:57.617
Okay, now that your body

00:01:57.617 --> 00:01:59.886
is saturated with oxygen

00:01:59.886 --> 00:02:02.355
you'd want to avoid any activity

00:02:02.355 --> 00:02:03.423
in order to slow down

00:02:03.423 --> 00:02:04.757
your heart rate.

00:02:04.757 --> 00:02:07.093
Just stay still as much as possible.

00:02:09.095 --> 00:02:10.563
After a five-minute

00:02:10.563 --> 00:02:12.098
exposure to water,

00:02:12.098 --> 00:02:13.967
your skin would prune,

00:02:13.967 --> 00:02:16.736
especially your fingers and toes.

00:02:16.736 --> 00:02:18.471
These aquatic wrinkles happen

00:02:18.471 --> 00:02:20.073
because of the narrowing

00:02:20.073 --> 00:02:22.108
of blood vessels in your skin.

00:02:22.108 --> 00:02:23.076
This shrinking

00:02:23.076 --> 00:02:25.979
is called digital vasoconstriction

00:02:25.979 --> 00:02:26.579
But,

00:02:26.579 --> 00:02:27.147
this is nothing

00:02:27.147 --> 00:02:29.048
you haven't experienced before.

00:02:29.048 --> 00:02:29.849
Let's keep going.

00:02:31.851 --> 00:02:33.286
If you spent these

00:02:33.286 --> 00:02:34.387
past twenty minutes

00:02:34.387 --> 00:02:36.823
without any breathing device

00:02:36.823 --> 00:02:38.525
there's a high chance

00:02:38.525 --> 00:02:40.793
you'd experience brain damage.

00:02:40.793 --> 00:02:42.228
The steady build-up of

00:02:42.228 --> 00:02:43.863
carbon dioxide in your blood

00:02:43.863 --> 00:02:44.864
would turn it

00:02:44.864 --> 00:02:47.000
into an acidic brew.

00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:48.201
Muscle spasms

00:02:48.201 --> 00:02:50.270
and disorientation could follow,

00:02:50.270 --> 00:02:50.937
as well as

00:02:50.937 --> 00:02:52.238
a racing heart

00:02:52.238 --> 00:02:53.740
and ultimately,

00:02:53.740 --> 00:02:54.841
death.

00:02:54.841 --> 00:02:56.609
So, to avoid all that,

00:02:56.609 --> 00:02:57.877
you'll need a scuba tank

00:02:57.877 --> 00:02:58.711
if you have

00:02:58.711 --> 00:02:59.679
any hope of

00:02:59.679 --> 00:03:00.880
finishing this challenge.

00:03:02.882 --> 00:03:04.083
Okay, now that you have some

00:03:04.083 --> 00:03:05.518
pure oxygen,

00:03:05.518 --> 00:03:06.352
you think this challenge

00:03:06.352 --> 00:03:07.954
will be easier right?

00:03:07.954 --> 00:03:08.755
Well,

00:03:08.755 --> 00:03:10.657
I’m not that sure.

00:03:10.657 --> 00:03:12.091
After seven hours

00:03:12.091 --> 00:03:13.126
of soaking,

00:03:13.126 --> 00:03:15.828
you could suffer from hypothermia.

00:03:15.828 --> 00:03:17.063
If the water temperature

00:03:17.063 --> 00:03:18.031
drops below

00:03:20.600 --> 00:03:22.268
your body temperature

00:03:22.268 --> 00:03:23.536
would dip down to

00:03:25.538 --> 00:03:26.706
or lower.

00:03:26.706 --> 00:03:28.141
You'd start to shiver,

00:03:28.141 --> 00:03:30.076
and your pulse would be weak

00:03:30.076 --> 00:03:31.044
The cold would

00:03:31.044 --> 00:03:32.545
affect your organs,

00:03:32.545 --> 00:03:33.980
especially your heart

00:03:33.980 --> 00:03:35.682
and nervous system.

00:03:35.682 --> 00:03:37.250
You could eventually

00:03:37.250 --> 00:03:39.219
go unconscious.

00:03:39.219 --> 00:03:40.820
With no warm-up,

00:03:40.820 --> 00:03:42.288
hypothermia can lead

00:03:42.288 --> 00:03:44.390
to your entire respiratory system

00:03:44.390 --> 00:03:45.491
shutting down

00:03:45.491 --> 00:03:47.594
and your death.

00:03:47.594 --> 00:03:49.495
So for your survival,

00:03:49.495 --> 00:03:50.597
the water temperature

00:03:50.597 --> 00:03:52.265
should be kept around

00:03:55.969 --> 00:03:58.471
Okay, after 24 hours of

00:03:58.471 --> 00:03:59.772
of underwater life.

00:03:59.772 --> 00:04:01.507
you’ll notice some bubbles

00:04:01.507 --> 00:04:03.176
forming on your skin.

00:04:03.176 --> 00:04:05.612
These are known as vesicles.

00:04:05.612 --> 00:04:07.113
They develop because

00:04:07.113 --> 00:04:08.615
water becomes trapped

00:04:08.615 --> 00:04:09.782
between your outer

00:04:09.782 --> 00:04:12.051
and middle layers of skin.

00:04:12.051 --> 00:04:13.786
They will continue to form

00:04:13.786 --> 00:04:15.421
the longer you stay in the water,

00:04:15.421 --> 00:04:18.458
and eventually burst.

00:04:18.458 --> 00:04:19.359
And now,

00:04:19.359 --> 00:04:20.159
as you finally

00:04:20.159 --> 00:04:21.127
finish this challenge, 

00:04:21.127 --> 00:04:23.029
and get out of the water, 

00:04:23.029 --> 00:04:24.030
your skin

00:04:24.030 --> 00:04:24.897
would start to

00:04:24.897 --> 00:04:25.732
peel away

00:04:25.732 --> 00:04:28.001
from the popped vesicles.

00:04:28.001 --> 00:04:29.569
You'd need medical attention

00:04:29.569 --> 00:04:30.470
immediately

00:04:30.470 --> 00:04:31.938
as you'd likely have

00:04:31.938 --> 00:04:33.106
a severe headache

00:04:33.106 --> 00:04:35.541
along with other health issues.

00:04:35.541 --> 00:04:36.843
Okay sure,

00:04:36.843 --> 00:04:38.144
you managed to make it

00:04:38.144 --> 00:04:40.613
out of this challenge alive but

00:04:40.613 --> 00:04:43.016
it definitely wouldn't be worth it.

00:04:43.016 --> 00:04:45.084
If you want to relax,

00:04:45.084 --> 00:04:45.752
I've heard

00:04:45.752 --> 00:04:47.687
that withstanding the cold

00:04:47.687 --> 00:04:49.589
can enhance your well-being.

00:04:49.589 --> 00:04:51.691
Want to give it a try?

00:04:51.691 --> 00:04:52.258
Okay,

00:04:52.258 --> 00:04:54.460
we'll see what that challenge brings

00:04:54.460 --> 00:04:56.529
on another episode of

